Enginehost: Ren'Py 8.5's Live2D start-up failure is raised, not noted.

onetime_init adds a note to the exception and drops it, then marks Live2D as
initialised, so has_live2d() answered True and a model loaded into NULL csm
function pointers (the crash 0004 describes). Re-raise it: has_live2d() is
False, and Live2D(...) shows the "Could not load Live2D" message.
--- a/renpy/gl2/live2d.py
+++ b/renpy/gl2/live2d.py
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ def onetime_init():
             raise Exception("Could not load Live2D. {} was not found.".format(dll))
     except Exception as e:
         e.add_note("Live2D Cubism 5.3 or later is required.")
+        raise
 
 
     did_onetime_init = True
